{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem","id":784066,"title":"Personal Totem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-11T05:17:09-08:00","id":784066,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Personal Totem","content":"My group recently picked up W:tF 2e and we're going through character creation. Needless to say, we're muddling through the rules and figuring stuff out as we go. But one question we couldn't really answer was in regard to Totems. The merit makes specific mention of personal Totems, but the Totem creation rules seem to be geared toward the pack Totem. If my player wants a personal totem, for 2 or 3 dots, the mechanical benefit seems to be pretty low. The player would only gain 1 experience to spend, and the spirit would be Rank 0 unless the player pumped 5 dots into the merit. Or at least that's how I'm interpreting the RAW. <br /> <br /> So, have I misunderstood something, or is the idea of a personal totem more of a story concept rather than a merit that comes with a decent mechanical benefit.<br /> <br /> please school me on this :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:22:49-08:00","id":784069,"title":"","content":"I think that's the only place that a personal totem is mentioned, so I'd suggest ignoring that element and focusing on the pack totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:34:17-08:00","id":784075,"title":"","content":"Pack totems are going to be more effective, just as werewolves are far more effective in packs than alone. A werewolf character might have a personal totem, but as you have noticed, the totem would be much weaker than a pack totem. Later on, the werewolf might save up Experiences and buy a bit more potent of a personal totem\u2014but the pack (and pack totem) might rightly wonder why she is not contributing to the group cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:35:04-08:00","id":784076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784069#post784069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's the only place that a personal totem is mentioned, so I'd suggest ignoring that element and focusing on the pack totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>We were leaning in that direction, but before we made a final decision I wanted to make sure I wasn't overlooking something simple. As I often do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:35:49-08:00","id":784077,"title":"","content":"Actually, there's another mention in the Touchstone section of a personal totem. I get the feeling that its more of a story thing than anything else. I build totems starting with 1 in each attribute section and at rank 1 - rank 0 spirits are effectively essence motes, which is innapropriate for play. <br /> <br /> So, a 1-dot personal totem would be weak, 2 in one attribute and 1 in the others, and could only carry 1 essence, but would have 1 numina. But it would be a character to interact with, much like a familar would be for a mage. And familars are insanely versatile and useful aids, so I wouldn't dismiss one out of hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:38:44-08:00","id":784079,"title":"","content":"A fair point, Claire. I hadn't considered how having and maintaining a personal Totem might look to the pack mates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:42:07-08:00","id":784082,"title":"","content":"Why would it look strange to pack mates? EXP are out of character resources, so no one thinks that you're rejecting one for the other. And why would anyone bat an eye at adopting another spirit to help the pack out in times of need?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:43:14-08:00","id":784083,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.. I hadn't been building the Totem with a starting dot in each Attribute. Is that a rule or a house rule MCN?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:47:09-08:00","id":784084,"title":"","content":"I could see a more paranoid pack being wary of a member who was diverting resources and efforts toward a personal totem rather than the pack's. We're playing in the Detroit setting, where Forsaken wolves are outnumbered by the Pure. Paranoia is probably pretty common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:48:58-08:00","id":784086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784083#post784083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm.. I hadn't been building the Totem with a starting dot in each Attribute. Is that a rule or a house rule MCN?</div> </div> </div> </div> Its how I understand the rules as writen, and consistant with how other things work. I could be mistaken, of course, but its worked so far for me, and hasn't broken the game in any way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:58:07-08:00","id":784096,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure that's a house rule. For the pack totem it's not really necessary. <br /> <br /> Really though, it might be better to model the personal totem as a spiritual ally. That way you can justify a boost in power for the same cost by removing the totem benefits, which really aren't worth it when it's just you contributing. It's basically just a one-experience discount on the totem merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T06:29:17-08:00","id":784119,"title":"","content":"I agree. Pack Totems exist primary to give mechanical benefits to all members of the Pack (even humans and those who join letter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T06:34:01-08:00","id":784122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784082#post784082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would it look strange to pack mates? EXP are out of character resources, so no one thinks that you're rejecting one for the other. And why would anyone bat an eye at adopting another spirit to help the pack out in times of need?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't know you're spending a game resource, no, but then, they don't know they're characters in a game. Within the story, though, those points are being justified somehow, right? So you are spending time and energy (quite literally) into cultivating something that benefits mostly you, rather than strengthening the very totem that supports the pack. As pack-oriented as werewolves are, I can see some taking umbrage to such actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T06:42:50-08:00","id":784129,"title":"","content":"Especially in the likely event the personal totem doesn't have the exact same goals and desires as the pack totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T08:28:23-08:00","id":784189,"title":"","content":"At the very least this confirms that I did not completely misinterpret the rules. I will check in with the player and see if he still wants to move ahead with the personal Totem knowing that there will be little mechanical benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T13:28:06-08:00","id":784322,"title":"","content":"You could just have the totem represented by the True Friend or Retainer merits. No mechanical benefits per se, but a spirit ally is always a valuable thing to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":".  Edit: typos 12-11-2015, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T14:50:16-08:00","id":784363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784122#post784122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't know you're spending a game resource, no, but then, they don't know they're characters in a game. Within the story, though, those points are being justified somehow, right? So you are spending time and energy (quite literally) into cultivating something that benefits mostly you, rather than strengthening the very totem that supports the pack. As pack-oriented as werewolves are, I can see some taking umbrage to such actions.</div> </div> </div> </div> How is that different than cultivating Allies, Contacts, Gifts, Rites, or fighting skills? Those are all benefiting you instead of the pack. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T15:25:54-08:00","id":784380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784322#post784322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could just have the totem represented by the True Friend or Retainer merits. No mechanical benefits per second, but a spirit ally is always a valuable thing to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a great solution. Very simple and applicable. I'm ashamed I didn't think of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T19:31:32-08:00","id":784493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784082#post784082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would it look strange to pack mates? EXP are out of character resources, so no one thinks that you're rejecting one for the other. And why would anyone bat an eye at adopting another spirit to help the pack out in times of need?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bale Hounds usually get recruited by spirits. So do some Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T04:40:43-08:00","id":784656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784493#post784493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bale Hounds usually get recruited by spirits. So do some Pure.</div> </div> </div> </div> This and that are separate issues. Werewolves deal with spirits on their own all the time. Or should we be suspicious of every time an Irraka goes off on his own, or the Itheur performs rites without the pack around him 24/7? Of course not, that'd be silly. Seriously, I can't even concieve of the kind of game you have to have where someone cultivating spirit allies is immediately suspect for turning Pure or Bale Hound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T05:51:34-08:00","id":784683,"title":"","content":"Why is this a sticking point for you? It's not that hard to understand.<br /> <br /> If one member of the pack spends too much time with her secondary totem it's bound to draw notice from the pack. The question isn't one of time spent specifically, because sure, a pack member might spend time maintaining relationships with Allies or some other group. The problem is one of alliegance. The relationship between a pack and a totem are paramount, throw another totem in the mix and exactly where the pack falls, the pack's totem falls and the personal totem falls in priority becomes a tricky question to answer. Might not sit well with most packs not knowing what'll happen when there's a conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T15:24:13-08:00","id":785022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784656#post784656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This and that are separate issues. Werewolves deal with spirits on their own all the time. Or should we be suspicious of every time an Irraka goes off on his own, or the Itheur performs rites without the pack around him 24/7? Of course not, that'd be silly. Seriously, I can't even concieve of the kind of game you have to have where someone cultivating spirit allies is immediately suspect for turning Pure or Bale Hound.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the difference between going with someone to school, and regularly eating lunch with them. Spirits, specially, love to influence shit. And some are a very, very bad influence.<br /> <br /> After all, &quot;Tell me who you go with, and I'll tell you who you are.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T03:43:04-08:00","id":785296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784683#post784683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is this a sticking point for you? It's not that hard to understand.<br /> <br /> If one member of the pack spends too much time with her secondary totem it's bound to draw notice from the pack. The question isn't one of time spent specifically, because sure, a pack member might spend time maintaining relationships with Allies or some other group. The problem is one of alliegance. The relationship between a pack and a totem are paramount, throw another totem in the mix and exactly where the pack falls, the pack's totem falls and the personal totem falls in priority becomes a tricky question to answer. Might not sit well with most packs not knowing what'll happen when there's a conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why is it a sticking point? 1) Define &quot;too much time.&quot; 2) Why should it be a question fo alliegence? Pack is family, not a hierarchy or chain of command, and you're not serving two masters here. In fact, you're not serving any masters here. 3) You have pack totems, different Tribal totems, and lodge totems that have never been an issue when taken together. Why is a fourth suddenly an issue? Hint - its not unless you make it one.<br /> <br /> What's hard to understand is this idea that having a personal totem absolutely must be antagonistic with the pack as a whole in some way. The idea of &quot;You're either with us or against us!&quot; is innately flawed here. Is synergy really that hard of a concept to grasp? That a personal totem might actually make the pack stronger and effective in some ways? Or that Uratha can have lives outside the pack?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785022#post785022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the difference between going with someone to school, and regularly eating lunch with them. Spirits, specially, love to influence shit. And some are a very, very bad influence.<br /> <br /> After all, &quot;Tell me who you go with, and I'll tell you who you are.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> And some are good influences. I fail to see your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T04:14:57-08:00","id":785309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785296#post785296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And some are good influences. I fail to see your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's debatable. There's a published module about a spirit of vice that ate some pack's totem and took it's place, and slowly corrupted them to insanity, for instance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T07:18:38-08:00","id":785377,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784075#post784075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the pack (and pack totem) <b>might</b> rightly wonder why she is not contributing to the group cause.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784079#post784079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fair point, Claire. I hadn't considered how having and maintaining a personal Totem <b>might </b>look to the pack mates.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=784129#post784129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially in the likely event the personal totem doesn't have the exact same goals and desires as the pack totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>That all seems fair to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785296#post785296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's hard to understand is this idea that having a personal totem absolutely must be antagonistic with the pack as a whole in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one said that. It was said that it <b>could</b> or<b> might </b>cause problems in a pack and that is not a controversial statement. I don't know why you're treating it like it is. Which is why I return to my question, why is this such a sticking point?<br /> <br /> To answer your earlier questions, I'm pretty sure Tribal priority and culture does cause conflict in packs at times, though because a pack's end goal is always the same it's usually resolved without issue. When a pack's Boneshadows insist on punishing a spirit that's broken the terms of their bargain, the rest of the pack might consider it unnecessary or too risky - especially if their plan worked out anyway. That might cause conflict. I could probably come up with a better example, but I'm tired.<br /> <br /> And quite a few lodges have it literally written into the fluff that the lodges priorities, methods, or reputation might cause conflict within their members packs. And Both lodges and tribes are organizations that have oversight through its other members and Uratha culture at large. Now if a pack member is in a lodge where he is the only member and the totem's motivations were known to him and him alone, it <b>might</b> cause suspicion.<br /> <br /> You can look to three of the book's Spirit touchstones for examples of personal totems gone wrong (The Buddy Spirit, The Lune, The Ambitious Totem). It's not a hard scenario to imagine, the book literally supports this, and you're treating it like it's some ridiculous idea that's been conjured out of thin air. It's not.<br /> <br /> Like Ephsy's lunch room example, this isn't even unique to Uratha, this is just a normal aspect of social groups.<br /> <br /> Listen, no one has said it's impossible for there to be a helpful personal totem. Literally, no one has said that. The most that's been said is that a personal totem's motivations <b>might</b> not align with the pack's. Not controversial. And no one has said that the relationship with a personal totem will definitively rankle the other members of a pack. Just that it <b>could</b>. Not controversial. The book's characterization of personal totems is in line with that interpretation, so to suggest that it's a thing that would or could occur often enough is also not controversial. So what are you objecting to? It sounds to me like you're making a thing out of nothing. This is what I meant by sticking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 12-13-2015, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T11:29:31-08:00","id":785488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785377#post785377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bListen, no one has said it's impossible for there to be a helpful personal totem. Literally, no one has said that. The most that's been said is that a personal totem's motivations <b>might</b> not align with the pack's. Not controversial. And no one has said that the relationship with a personal totem will definitively rankle the other members of a pack. Just that it <b>could</b>. Not controversial. The book's characterization of personal totems is in line with that interpretation, so to suggest that it's a thing that would or could occur often enough is also not controversial. So what are you objecting to? It sounds to me like you're making a thing out of nothing. This is what I meant by sticking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand you meant your post to be neutral, but I got the same impression as MCN and wondered why you were placing so much emphasis on the negative possibilities of having a personal totem. He definitely was not alone. In any case, thank you for clarifying your position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T11:51:25-08:00","id":785498,"title":"","content":"Mine? That's good, I guess. Before I said anything, MCN had already seemed very confused by the idea that a personal totem would ever be a problem. At times he seemed outright insistent that it shouldn't be. I was responding directly to that notion, hence my focus on the problems that could and likely would often arrive from the inclusion of a personal totem into a pack's dynamic. That's all. I mean, the book gives us three examples right off the bat for a reason.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 12-13-2015, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T12:28:55-08:00","id":785511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785498#post785498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mine? Before I said anything, MCN had already seemed very confused by the idea that a personal totem would ever be a problem. At times he seemed outright insistent that it shouldn't be. I was responding directly to that notion, hence my focus on the problems that could and likely would often arrive from the inclusion of a personal totem into a pack's dynamic. That's all. I mean, the book gives us three examples right off the bat for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a baseline all social merits have the potential to create problems. Claire's post seems to place unusual emphasis upon the negative aspects of having a personal totem. MCN seems to be wondering why Claire thinks having a personal totem would cause <b>MORE</b> problems than any other social merit. You supported Claire's position and escalated the issue with &quot;Why is this a sticking point for you? It's not that hard to understand.&quot;<br /> <br /> But you clarified your position. So it is all good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T13:13:27-08:00","id":785534,"title":"","content":"Nearly every merit got a drawback. Drawbacks provide drama. Drama is good for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T18:19:27-08:00","id":785664,"title":"","content":"Totem spirits provide power and patronage in return for the same from their packs. They are generally proud. At the very least, they all take personal investment in the pack that supports them. Spirits, like their pack allies, are predators. Other spirits are competitors. Additional totems are competing for the same resources. Even if they're all working together, I think many\u2014but certainly not all\u2014totems would get a bit chippy about it. Would a Greek god take umbrage at a worshiper deciding to take on a second god of equal (or perhaps greater) personal importance? In some ways it's the same here.<br /> <br /> Cultivating Allies, Contacts, or personal power all benefit the pack as a whole. They improve the werewolf's position as a hunter, and thus the pack's position. On the surface, so does cultivating additional totems, but it's the context that matters. It's cultivating a relationship with a different patron spirit, granting it power and importance in the hunt, thereby taking away the same gain from the original totem spirit. Every time you favor your personal totem, even if no offense is meant thereby, you're choosing it instead of the pack totem. I can see that being a problem in a way that a werewolf having her own mortal friends or family are not.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be a universal case, though. For example, a totem that is part of a choir, or perhaps coming to lead their own brood thanks to the patronage of the pack, might encourage bringing another member into the fold. Though spirits are creatures of Darwinistic hierarchy, so the pack totem probably has a vested interest in remaining the alpha predator among the totems. While it's <i>possible </i>to make all of this work, it's also a potentially volatile situation capable of boiling over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T04:42:50-08:00","id":785894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785377#post785377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWhich is why I return to my question, why is this such a sticking point?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm disagreeing on the negative focus, which I'm saying should be on par with anything else. Of course anything might have a drawback. But the way I'm reading it is that people are assuming that the problems (rivalry, turning into Pure) with personal totems are going to be the norm. Even you are saying &quot;likely.&quot; I disagree on the &quot;likely&quot; aspect. There's no reason that we have to have a personal totem that's going to try and drive me to the Pure or Bale Hounds.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785664#post785664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Would a Greek god take umbrage at a worshiper deciding to take on a second god of equal (or perhaps greater) personal importance? In some ways it's the same here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering that greco-roman socities include family gods and personal patrons? I'm going to have to go with a resounding &quot;no!&quot; For the most part, as long as you remembered to give them their due, the gods didn't care if you didn't give a second god their separate due as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's cultivating a relationship with a different patron spirit, granting it power and importance in the hunt, thereby taking away the same gain from the original totem spirit. Every time you favor your personal totem, even if no offense is meant thereby, you're choosing it instead of the pack totem. I can see that being a problem in a way that a werewolf having her own mortal friends or family are not. </div> </div> </div> False dichotomy. That's like saying you can't love two people equally. And, last time I checked, I love my family all equally. I don't suddenly love my sister less because she just gave birth to a new son. I was raised Roman Catholic, though I don't practice anymore. I had a personal saint patron, my church has a different one, and then there was the Trinity. All were given prayer and observations. It can be done <i>in real life</i>. Why should a game be different?<br /> <br /> I reject your statement in its entirety. I reject that having a personal totem automatically means a volative combination. Yes, there will be some drama, just as their is drama between Tribal, Lodge, and Pack totems, but they are all balanceable, and make for a stronger whole. Time may be a limited reasource, but it doesn't mean that you're choosing someone over another. There's nothing more to discuss on the matter. If that's how you want to run the game, that's fine, more power to you. However, there is nothing instrictively insulting or volative about this for every game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T04:47:24-08:00","id":785896,"title":"","content":"Actually, in real life our ancestors definitely worshipped multiple gods and totem spirits without problems. It's a very Judeo-Christian notion that there's going to be problems.<br /> <br /> If a character pays into tribe and lodge totems (through status) then there is little problem with having a personal totem. Totems are partners and associates, you honor them and pay them tribute in return for favors. You don't worship them (at least not the way Judeo-Christians understand the concept). They do not get jealous of one another in the manner folks are suggesting. If they did, the big bad tribal totem would simply gobble the smaller ones up. Anyway, that's an understanding from a shaman's point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T06:21:17-08:00","id":785931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785664#post785664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Greek god take umbrage at a worshiper deciding to take on a second god of equal (or perhaps greater) personal importance? In some ways it's the same here.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was common practice to pay your respects to any god that might be relevant to a situation. An individual city would often have a patron, but it was always important to pay your respects to the others. In fact, not paying your respects to the other gods would be a (theoretically) quick way to earn some divine retribution.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T08:27:11-08:00","id":785992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785931#post785931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was common practice to pay your respects to any god that might be relevant to a situation. An individual city would often have a patron, but it was always important to pay your respects to the others. In fact, not paying your respects to the other gods would be a (theoretically) quick way to earn some divine retribution.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. Not sure how this whole thread came about. The pack is one aspect of a werewolf's life, but so is the tribe, lodge, and self. Totems at every level aren't just fine, they are probably the norm. Werewolves are actually incomplete without one (or more) personal totems. <br /> <br /> Which brings me to another point. IRL people who practice shamanism do not limit themselves to one overarching totem. Tribes have multiple totems and people have multiple personal totems. But in game most folks are limited to one totem per level (one for tribe, one for lodge, one for pack, and one for self). From a mechanical side, this simplifies things but on the metaphysical (or really metaspiritual) level one probably shouldn't read these limitations as being caused by some kind of jealousy on the part of the spirits. Rather the totem - tribe/lodge/pack/person relationship is one of kindred spirits and thereby kinship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T12:37:16-08:00","id":786135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785894#post785894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reject your statement in its entirety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785894#post785894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing more to discuss on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm preeeeeetty sure you're not the final authority on what can be discussed and when.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785894#post785894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's how you want to run the game, that's fine, more power to you. However, there is nothing instrictively insulting or volative about this for every game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said there was, so ... yeah. Have a nice day?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T12:43:48-08:00","id":786142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=785931#post785931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was common practice to pay your respects to any god that might be relevant to a situation. An individual city would often have a patron, but it was always important to pay your respects to the others. In fact, not paying your respects to the other gods would be a (theoretically) quick way to earn some divine retribution.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. I guess what I meant was more like having a temple devoted pretty much solely to the honor of Zeus. Then building a statue of another god in that temple right next to Zeus' and splitting your time between Zeus and, say, Hades. Zeus might take some offense to it. But then, maybe the Greek gods aren't the best examples because they were jerks.<br /> <br /> The references to real-life shamanism\u2014something to which I am myself drawn due to Native roots I have yet to really connect with\u2014do bring up a good point, though. I never said every such multiple-totem situation would necessarily cause drama, but it could be a factor for some stories. Spirits can be vain, selfish, greedy, and arrogant, just like mortals can, so it could easily be a thing. But I'd be okay with the assumption that in most cases, it's just a part of how the supernatural ecosystem looks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T17:24:15-08:00","id":786368,"title":"","content":"Ironically building temples right next to each was pretty common. That's why they called them complexes. You'd also have a couple of shrines for the house, shrines on the street corner, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> I honestly think you're blowing the whole jealousy angle up way out of proportion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T18:15:59-08:00","id":786395,"title":"","content":"She's not saying building temples besides each other. She's saying erecting a statue in another's temple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T18:27:37-08:00","id":786403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=786395#post786395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's not saying building temples besides each other. She's saying erecting a statue in another's temple.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was also done. Especially in Asian religions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T18:58:35-08:00","id":786418,"title":"","content":"Here is where the issue with a personal totem comes up. Yes every werewolf has a tribal totem, and their behavior is influenced slightly by their Tribal Oath. Yes you have the pack totem, where things get more hairy. A packs behavior is heavily influenced by their totem. Have a totem of war? You are going to be spending time going into battle and following the pack Bane of picking fights with every tough bastard that comes along. When you get to the subject of a personal totem, how is it going to work? A totem isn't a spirit ally, it is a spirit that the werewolf in question holds at least partial fealty to in return for benefits from said spirit. When you already have a pack totem 2 conflicts arise.<br /> <br /> Conflict between the pack and pack mate. The pack has already dedicated a huge amount towards their current pack totem, one that influences their style and behavior. Why would any pack mate stop doing that to form a totem bond with another spirit? The pack, now has to worry about their totem being offended, how this new totems interests may clash with the pack totems, and whether or not the pack mate will have the interest of the pack at heart.<br /> <br /> Conflict from the totem. Spirits are not nice buddy buddy kinds of beings. You take a personal totem and your pack totem will have NONE of that shit. It didn't bind itself to a pack of werewolves for shits and giggle, it did so because the pack furthers it's interests and gives it a crap ton of essence in doing so. Now some werewolf is going to take time away from the pack totem to go put effort into another spirit? One of three things is going to happen, most likely two.<br /> <br /> 1. Pack totem is going to remove his favor from the werewolf in question. This is almost a foregone conclusion. If your pack totem sees you running off forming another totem bond and ignoring it for your new spirit, be prepared to lose the mechanical benefits of the pack totem.<br /> <br /> 2. Pack totem is going to attack your personal totem and likely destroy it. Your pack totem is not most likely not going to sit by while some low rank spirit comes along and tries to take away from the pack it has been working with to further it's interests.<br /> <br /> 3. The whole pack will suffer loss of their totems blessing. Less likely but still possible. Some especially proud spirits will blame the ENTIRE pack for not stopping this werewolf from dedicating said amount of time to furthering it as a totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","user":"Heroofthemists","date":". 12-14-2015, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T01:27:43-08:00","id":786576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=786418#post786418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conflict between the pack and pack mate. The pack has already dedicated a huge amount towards their current pack totem, one that influences their style and behavior. Why would any pack mate stop doing that to form a totem bond with another spirit? The pack, now has to worry about their totem being offended, how this new totems interests may clash with the pack totems, and whether or not the pack mate will have the interest of the pack at heart.<br /> <br /> Conflict from the totem. Spirits are not nice buddy buddy kinds of beings. You take a personal totem and your pack totem will have NONE of that shit. It didn't bind itself to a pack of werewolves for shits and giggle, it did so because the pack furthers it's interests and gives it a crap ton of essence in doing so. Now some werewolf is going to take time away from the pack totem to go put effort into another spirit? One of three things is going to happen, most likely two.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you are talking about sounds more like a Fire-Touched Pack. Depending on how you spend your merits a totem could be a spirit ally, a true friend, or several other things. You can absolutely have a totem that is intensely jealous about their pack and does not wish them to share any time with others, but that is going to depend entirely on the motivations of the pack and what kind of spirit the totem is.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Pack Perspective</b></u><b>:</b> Sometimes totems can be forced upon a pack, but most of the time the pack is going to ask a spirit to become their totem or be approached by a spirit who wants to strike a bargain. This means the power of choice lies with the pack, who are probably either choosing to work with that spirit because it will bring them great power or because they can get along with the spirit. A Forsaken pack might put up with an asshole spirit for the sake of power, but this is going to depend heavily on what the pack needs and how they feel about assholes. Storm Lords might endure a jealous totem because it shows their dedication to the cause. Blood Talons might not accept a totem that refuses to work with others. Iron Masters might tell the spirit to stop with the controlling boyfriend shit.<br /> <br /> Since most packs are not going to put up with an asshole, that leaves spirits that are willing to exchange benefits like a business arrangement or spirits they genuinely like. This means that most totems are going to be at least tolerable and possibly even decent. If the spirit starts behaving in a way that is uncool then the pack has the right to ask them to shape up, and if the bad behavior continues then they may drop the totem entirely and seek out some other spirit. Particularly brutal packs might take their totem down a dark alley in the Shadow and beat some sense into the spirit until it agrees to cooperate.<br /> <br /> The important thing is that Forsaken packs are going to have actual relationships with their Totems. It's going to be a two way street where both parties may do things that annoy the other, and sometimes there might even be some serious drama. But as long as things generally stay positive then everything works out. That is what friendship is all about.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Spirit Perspective</b></u><b>:</b> Maybe a spirit dreams of bossing around a bunch of werewolves, then forcing the pack to serve them and becoming Pure. Good for them. Most spirits are not going to be that lucky. They may be pretty obsessive about what they want, but if they have a couple of ranks under their belt they are going to be smarter than your average mote. The kind of spirits that end up as Forsaken totems are going to understand that werewolves can protect it from other spirits that might want to eat it, and provide it with food and power in exchange for spiritual favor. As long as it gets more out of the bargain than it loses, it is probably not going to want to casually break that pact.<br /> <br /> These middle rank spirits are going to be like teenagers and that is okay. They are going to push the boundaries and see how much they can get away with, and if the pack lets that happen then they are going to keep pushing until they dominate the pack like you are suggesting. Most Forsaken packs are not going to let that happen. The spirit is going to be sullen for a while but eventually will learn that it cannot be a total asshole without the risk of losing that protection. Lower rank spirits might even need constant reinforcement of this lesson.<br /> <br /> The type of spirit also plays a huge role. A lion totem spirit is probably not going to be cool with someone's personal deer totem, and much like the scorpion that stung the lion, the lion is going to have a hard time resisting the urge to eat the deer. The pack has every reason to wonder why someone is bringing in a deer totem to a lion pack. But that same lion totem is probably not going to have a big issue with someone else having another lion spirit as long as this new personal totem understands the hierarchy. Spirits of herd animals or community spirits are probably going to have the easiest time cooperating with personal totems. A computer spirit might be ecstatic about having someone else to network with, which would be confusing as hell to your personal frog totem. A warfare spirit might welcome personal totems with open arms, while expecting them to behave like good soldiers.<br /> <br /> The higher in rank a spirit is, the more likely it is going to be part of a tithing network. It has a boss it needs to send essence to, and as long as something particularly delicious does not come along it should have no problems with lesser spirits hanging out -- provided they are contributing essence to the pack totem as their own tithe.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Storyteller Perspective</b></u><b>:</b> At the end of the day, the player and the storyteller should sit down together and discuss what kind of story they want to tell about the personal totem. If both parties think a story about jealousy and power would be interesting, then that is what's going to happen. If both parties think a story about business contracts or friendship would be interesting, then that is how the relationship is going to play out. The personal totem might be put into peril when the story demands it, but the majority of scenes involving the personal totem are going to be about the things the player and storyteller agreed upon.<br /> <br /> It's also okay for a storyteller to say no. Much like bringing a paladin into a group full of thieves, a storyteller should let a player know if his personal totem is going to be a problem or not before those experience points are spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 12-15-2015, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T05:35:55-08:00","id":786659,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the mechanics of the game end up being that the character has an additional benefit and also an additional ban. Anything else, especially ideas that the totems will be jealous of one another or that the ban of a war totem requires you to psychotically pick fights aren't supported by the text or logic. If it was simply a matter of fealty then there would be no pack totems (or lodge totems), there would only be tribal totems. (They are the kings.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T06:14:45-08:00","id":786673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=786659#post786659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the mechanics of the game end up being that the character has an additional benefit and also an additional ban. Anything else, especially ideas that the totems will be jealous of one another or that the ban of a war totem requires you to psychotically pick fights aren't supported by the text or logic. If it was simply a matter of fealty then there would be no pack totems (or lodge totems), there would only be tribal totems. (They are the kings.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except this isn't a mechanical discussion. This is a discussion about the complications of having a personal totem on top of a pack totem. Tribal totems are so far removed from the character's literal presence, that actually being -noticed- by them should be scary, in an on itself. All the things myself and Claire exposed on are based on how the setting has been handling totems since the first edition corebook. <br /> <br /> Spirits are alien. They aren't your friends. The relationship is symbiotic, at best. And if your relationship with another spirit is seen as a stick on the wheel of a bigger spirit, then that spirit is going to take matters upon it's own paws/tentacles/flagellar movement appendixes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T06:19:46-08:00","id":786678,"title":"","content":"I don't believe I'd have a personal totem offer a mechanical benefit beyond having a spirit you're 'close' with. It would be more of an ally or cheerleader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T08:24:47-08:00","id":786733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=786678#post786678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe I'd have a personal totem offer a mechanical benefit beyond having a spirit you're 'close' with. It would be more of an ally or cheerleader.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a personal totem does not need any mechanical representation. But you can attach many different social merits to your personal totem (or even a touchstone) if you want. There is a lot of flexibility here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T08:38:50-08:00","id":786740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=786673#post786673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except this isn't a mechanical discussion. This is a discussion about the complications of having a personal totem on top of a pack totem. Tribal totems are so far removed from the character's literal presence, that actually being -noticed- by them should be scary, in an on itself. All the things myself and Claire exposed on are based on how the setting has been handling totems since the first edition corebook. <br /> <br /> Spirits are alien. They aren't your friends. The relationship is symbiotic, at best. And if your relationship with another spirit is seen as a stick on the wheel of a bigger spirit, then that spirit is going to take matters upon it's own paws/tentacles/flagellar movement appendixes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that they aren't as alien as you make them out to be. Idigam are alien. Spirits are well described and we know all about interactions that Werewolves have with them. They respect renown. They can be bribed through Chimenage. They can be dominated into giving essence or being stuffed into a fetish. Werewolves entire cultural identity is built around interacting with spirits. This pack/personal dichtomy is frankly weird. Try thinking of a personal totem as more of a personal spirit guide which can be expressed a number of ways but which should not automatically set a character up for some kind of group punishment. <br /> <br /> Try considering the troupe and the type of story everyone wants to tell. Only pursue conflict between totems if that's the kind of story that interests everyone (especially the person with the personal totem). Otherwise personal totems should not be a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T11:52:51-08:00","id":786830,"title":"","content":"Oh man, if I had a freaking penny by the amount of times I've read in several different books how fucking alien spirits are. Literally amoral entities governed by draconian set of inner rules. Please, go read up on the setting and then come back.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: Not even Ithaeur can ever hope to fully figure out a spirit. They're constantly evolving sons of bitches, because they are what they eat. There's nothing static about the Shadow, or how it's developments play out in a territory. Go check out the Hunting Grounds. The guys in Detroit were pretty fucking cozy with their arrangements with them, till the Pure figured out a loophole. Yes, you can have spirit allies. Till they give you enough rope to hang yourself with. Why?<br /> <br /> Because they're predators, and the Shadow is a Darwinian dog-eats-dog Hellscape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:09:45-08:00","id":786883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=786830#post786830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man, if I had a freaking penny by the amount of times I've read in several different books how fucking alien spirits are. Literally amoral entities governed by draconian set of inner rules. Please, go read up on the setting and then come back.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: Not even Ithaeur can ever hope to fully figure out a spirit. They're constantly evolving sons of bitches, because they are what they eat. There's nothing static about the Shadow, or how it's developments play out in a territory. Go check out the Hunting Grounds. The guys in Detroit were pretty fucking cozy with their arrangements with them, till the Pure figured out a loophole. Yes, you can have spirit allies. Till they give you enough rope to hang yourself with. Why?<br /> <br /> Because they're predators, and the Shadow is a Darwinian dog-eats-dog Hellscape.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So is Earth and so are people. Not seeing your problem and really beginning to drift into the weird territory of dictating how other people play.<br /> <br /> I've read Forsaken 2nd ed. I'm not seeing the issue you are. Maybe the problem is your using spirits that are too alien to be relatable pack totems. Maybe your approach is too confrontational. I don't know but nothing in the book necessitates the conflict you're promulgating. It's merely one read. You guys can debate it if you want but I'd talk it over with your players before you slam them over the head with this. If you bait and switch with totems folks will rightfully get upset because you'll basically be railroading them.<br /> <br /> You can note the drawback to them, &quot;Being tied to a totem leaves a character beholden to the totem. If your character angers the totem, the invested totem points fade. This may require the pack to re-negotiate their totem advantage. The points can return if your character makes reparations with the totem, but must be re-purchased.&quot; But you shouldn't purposefully cheat them out of having both a personal totem and a pack totem just because you believe conflict between the two totems is inevitable. Afterall the merit starts with, &quot;Your character has a relationship to a totem spirit, either personally or to a pack totem.&quot;<br /> <br /> At the end of the day you're adding additional drawbacks and/or screwing around with the sanctity of merits. There's nothing wrong with this in and of itself but you should go for player buy-in before you put them in a situation where one of the totems has to go. If they aren't interested in your story idea for totem conflict then you'll have to suck it up and deal with it because by the book they can purchase both merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:23:45-08:00","id":786891,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think the whole personal totem thing is a bit of a red herring - I'm as surprised as anyone to know it's even referenced in the text. Most personal relationships with spirits that are not pack or Lodge totems will be as Spiritual Touchstones, Allies or Contacts rather than a mini Totem merit.<br /> <br /> To promote good holiday season feelings, and on a tangent, I am trying to sort something that'll be a bit of a Werewolf-y Christmas\u200b Gift for you Werewolf fans - can't guarantee it'll happen before Xmas but I hope it does <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:26:16-08:00","id":786895,"title":"","content":"Thank you for making something useful come out of this thread. It's truly a Festivus miracle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T15:30:21-08:00","id":786991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=786673#post786673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except this isn't a mechanical discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>This did start out as a mechanical discussion. It just quickly changed into something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T15:46:41-08:00","id":786999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=786883#post786883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So is Earth and so are people. Not seeing your problem and really beginning to drift into the weird territory of dictating how other people play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here, read some setting:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/s5XZ3Vu.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/a3XHQKy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/ep9F4ky.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/uhe6OKe.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T15:56:15-08:00","id":787003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=786999#post786999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here, read some setting:</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in those setting descriptions suggests that a character cannot have a personal totem within the pack. It does enforce, however, that Spirits have Orange/Blue morality and that while you might be really good allies and True Friend with a, say, Fire Spirit, it's still a freaking Fire Spirit and might show gratitude in the most inconvientent way possible for your character.<br /> <br /> Spirits are bizarre and aren't human at all, but that doesn't preclude them from having relationships with your characters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T16:12:18-08:00","id":787011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=787003#post787003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing in those setting descriptions suggests that a character cannot have a personal totem within the pack. It does enforce, however, that Spirits have Orange/Blue morality and that while you might be really good allies and True Friend with a, say, Fire Spirit, it's still a freaking Fire Spirit and might show gratitude in the most inconvientent way possible for your character.<br /> <br /> Spirits are bizarre and aren't human at all, but that doesn't preclude them from having relationships with your characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read my posts: I never said they couldn't. I said there would indeed, be complications from that. Which would generate drama, which is good for the game.<br /> <br /> An example of a Helion being released from the webs of an Azlu has the spirit burning the face of the Ithaeur to the point of permanent disfiguration so that &quot;Other Spirits know of your great service to me&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 12-15-2015, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T17:57:21-08:00","id":787060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=787011#post787011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read my posts: I never said they couldn't. I said there would indeed, be complications from that. Which would generate drama, which is good for the game. An example of a Helion being released from the webs of an Azlu has the spirit burning the face of the Ithaeur to the point of permanent disfiguration so that &quot;Other Spirits know of your great service to me&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot find a single post in this thread suggesting that there should be no complications. The issue is that some posters have (accidentally or intentionally) suggested that personal totems will cause <b>MORE</b> drama than the baseline inherent in any other social merit.<br /> <br /> One poster is even suggesting that most pack totems are going to flip out and murder personal totems or disown their pack. This might be true for a few totems, but most totems are going to be far more reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 12-15-2015, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T18:00:44-08:00","id":787062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=787060#post787060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot find a single post in this thread suggesting that there should be no complications. The issue is that some posters have (accidentally or intentionally) suggested that personal totems will cause <b>MORE</b> drama than the baseline inherent in any other social merit.<br /> <br /> One poster is even suggesting that most pack totems are going to flip out and murder personal totems or disown their pack. Which is a big &quot;NO&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno on the disowning, but eating another spirit, if the target looks succulent enough? I don't see why it wouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T18:47:43-08:00","id":787075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=787062#post787062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno on the disowning, but eating another spirit, if the target looks succulent enough? I don't see why it wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the same reasons that most sociopaths don't become mass murderers. They figure out they are safer with allies, even if they are incapable of completely trusting those allies. Rank 0 - 1 are not going to be able to figure this out, but most totems are not Rank 0 - 1. Rank 2 is where things start getting interesting, because even my dog can understand this concept. Rank 3 is getting into the political situation and understands tithing.<br /> <br /> But I noticed you used the phrase 'if the target looks succulent enough'. We're not talking about a 'target that looks succulent enough', but personal totems in general. So let's use a couple of examples -- our hypothetical pack has a cat totem:<br /> <br /> Internet personal totem - Why would the cat totem care? As long as the cat totem is getting more than enough essence to keep itself happy, at best it might be interested in this 'meme' thing.<br /> <br /> Bear personal totem - Larger bear spirits thematically have great courage, and a big cat totem might be interested in this. But it is not really up the alley of the cat totem. Also it helps the cat totem stay safe, and makes a pack member happy which also helps the cat totem stay safe. The bear totem gets left alone.<br /> <br /> Mouse personal totem - Who the hell brings a mouse personal totem to a cat pack? There is no avoiding some drama here -- Rank 2 means there is probably going to be some Tom &amp; Jerry action going on, but Rank 3+ and higher is going to be more open to bargaining. It might hold off on eating that mouse personal totem as long as the pack member brings it an extra point of essence every other day. This is good business. A constant stream of essence is better than a single meal of essence, and Rank 3+ is better at dealing with instant gratification.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T20:33:32-08:00","id":787124,"title":"","content":"By succulent, yes, I mean most spirits won't go around eating whatever pops in front of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T22:42:46-08:00","id":787165,"title":"","content":"If you want a personal totem and are willing to spend Merit dots on it, go ahead. It will be relatively weak, but it can grow. There may be drama and rivalry between it and the pack totem, but they'll both cope. Why? Because 1) They're both beholden to the pack for things they can't get on their own, and packs have been known to ditch unsuitable totems, and 2) You paid Merit dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T05:48:51-08:00","id":788012,"title":"","content":"I know this is a bit off to left field, but since the original post was asking if there was any decent mechanical benefit to a personal totem I just thought I'd mention the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide. It's a 1st ed. book, but it does offer an option where you take a personal totem and it merges with you, giving you a larger mechanical benefit than normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","name":"Akaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T05:52:10-08:00","id":788018,"title":"","content":"Blasphemies has some rules for personal totems, as they act as intermediaries between Bale Hounds and the Maeljin under the Dark Pantheism option. Though these are manifestations of the vastly powerful Maeljin and even the weakest is of Jaggling rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T16:43:22-08:00","id":788398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=786891#post786891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To promote good holiday season feelings, and on a tangent, I am trying to sort something that'll be a bit of a Werewolf-y Christmas\u200b Gift for you Werewolf fans - can't guarantee it'll happen before Xmas but I hope it does <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>...which is now submitted to Stew, so we'll see what he thinks of it and if it'll appear any time soon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T17:01:01-08:00","id":788405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=788398#post788398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...which is now submitted to Stew, so we'll see what he thinks of it and if it'll appear any time soon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully it's one before actual Christmas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:20:34-08:00","id":789299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Akaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=788012#post788012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is a bit off to left field, but since the original post was asking if there was any decent mechanical benefit to a personal totem I just thought I'd mention the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide. It's a 1st ed. book, but it does offer an option where you take a personal totem and it merges with you, giving you a larger mechanical benefit than normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great news! I never even thought to look there. I'm going to check that out right now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T13:54:43-08:00","id":791780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=788405#post788405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hopefully it's one before actual Christmas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And it is! Part 1 of the Gift design article is now up on the blog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T15:59:33-08:00","id":792405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784066-personal-totem?p=791780#post791780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it is! Part 1 of the Gift design article is now up on the blog.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really love the Screaming Moon Gifts. I know it is casually mentioned in the Cahalith section of the book, but until reading the Screaming Moon Gifts it never really cemented itself into my mind:<br /> <br /> <b>During the Hunt, the job of the Cahalith is to <i>SCARE THE PREY.</i></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}